==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*deuzą}}, from {{inh|ang|ine-pro|*dʰewsóm}}.

Germanic cognates include {{cog|ofs|diār}}, {{cog|osx|dior}}, {{cog|odt|dier}}, {{cog|goh|tior}}, {{cog|non|dýr}}, [[w:Gothic language|Gothic]] ''[[𐌳𐌹𐌿𐍃|dius]]''. The Indo-European root also led to {{cog|lt|dvēsti}}, [[w:Russian language|Russian]] ''[[душа|duša]]''.

